<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Sallarid dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">919 CE – 1062 CE (approx.) · capital Tarom</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Daylamite dynasty from the castle of Tarom that ruled Azerbaijan and much of Armenia in the mid-10th century, part of the Iranian intermezzo.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sallarid-emirate">Sallarids</a>, also called Musafirids or Langarids, were lords of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarom">Tarom</a> with their stronghold at Shamiran on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qezel-ozan">Qezel Ozan</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-musafir">Muhammad ibn Musafir</a> married into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/justanid-dynasty">Justanid dynasty</a> and became the leading power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daylam">Daylam</a>. In 941 his sons Marzuban and Wahsudan seized control of their father's lands, and Marzuban took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marzuban-ibn-muhammad">Marzuban ibn Muhammad</a> ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabriz">Tabriz</a>, extending his authority over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/caucasian-albania">Arran</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/shirvanshah-state">Shirvan</a> and Armenian princes and defending against the Rus raid on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barda">Barda'a</a> in 943 to 944. Sources say he favoured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> missionaries. Daylamite soldiers formed the core of his army. In 948 he was captured by the Buyid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rukn-al-dawla">Rukn al-Dawla</a>, and his family's hold on <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> weakened in later succession quarrels.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rawwadid-emirate">Rawwadid Emirate</a>, while the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sallarid-emirate">Sallarids</a> kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarom">Tarom</a>. In 1062 the Seljuk sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughril">Tughril</a> took the submission of the last ruler, ending the dynasty.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sallarid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Sallarid dynasty" width="320" height="221"><figcaption>Image: Arab_Hafez, edited by HistoryofIran (me). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SallaridMapHistoryofIran.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>919 CE – 1062 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tarom</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Muhammad ibn Musafir, Marzuban ibn Muhammad, Wahsudan ibn Muhammad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Daylami, Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a>, <a href="/countries/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sallarids, Musafirids, Langarids</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=990&amp;focus=sallarid-dynasty" aria-label="Sallarid dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5882 804 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sallarid dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6202 1060L6240 1107M6202 1060L6153 1065M6202 1060L6481 1127"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6240 1107h0M6153 1065h0M6481 1127h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6202 1060h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6202 1060h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=990&amp;focus=sallarid-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

